{"name":"Shalimar","hex":"#f8f6a8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Shalimar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in Okaloosa County, Florida, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Shalimar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shalimar Bagh, Srinagar","blocks":[{"text":"Shalimar Bagh is a Mughal garden in Srinagar, Indian-administered Jammu and Kashmir, located at the northeast of Dal Lake. It is also known as Shalimar Garden, Farah Baksh, and Faiz Baksh. The other famous shoreline garden in the vicinity is Nishat Bagh, 'The Garden of Delight'. The garden was built by Mughal emperor Jahangir in 1619 and is considered the high point of Mughal horticulture. It is now a public park and also referred to as the \"Crown of Srinagar\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Shalimar_Bagh_1.jpg/330px-Shalimar_Bagh_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shalimar_Bagh%2C_Srinagar"},{"title":"Shalimar (perfume)","blocks":[{"text":"Shalimar is a perfume originally created by Jacques Guerlain in 1921 for French perfume and cosmetics house Guerlain. In production continuously since 1925, Shalimar is currently a flagship product for Guerlain."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b0/Perfume_Shalimar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shalimar_(perfume)"},{"title":"Shalimar (1978 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Shalimar is a 1978 bilingual Indo-American film, written and directed by Krishna Shah. The film stars Dharmendra, Zeenat Aman and Sir Rex Harrison, alongside John Saxon, Sylvia Miles, Shammi Kapoor and O. P. Ralhan."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/Shalimar_1978_film.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shalimar_(1978_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/A_view_of_Shalimar_Bagh_in_Srinagar.jpg/500px-A_view_of_Shalimar_Bagh_in_Srinagar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/A_view_of_Shalimar_Bagh_in_Srinagar.jpg/1280px-A_view_of_Shalimar_Bagh_in_Srinagar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/A_view_of_Shalimar_Bagh_in_Srinagar.jpg/500px-A_view_of_Shalimar_Bagh_in_Srinagar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A view of Shalimar Bagh","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_view_of_Shalimar_Bagh_in_Srinagar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/The_entrance_to_Shalimar_Bagh%2C_Srinagar.jpg/500px-The_entrance_to_Shalimar_Bagh%2C_Srinagar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/The_entrance_to_Shalimar_Bagh%2C_Srinagar.jpg/500px-The_entrance_to_Shalimar_Bagh%2C_Srinagar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Entrance channel to Shalimar Bagh from Dal Lake, 1864 view","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_entrance_to_Shalimar_Bagh%2C_Srinagar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Shalimar_Gardens%2C_Kashmir..jpg/500px-Shalimar_Gardens%2C_Kashmir..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Shalimar_Gardens%2C_Kashmir..jpg/500px-Shalimar_Gardens%2C_Kashmir..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View of Shalimar Bagh","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShalimar_Gardens%2C_Kashmir..jpg"},{"srcset":"https://t